WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.289
Graduation here means shipped, not binge-watched.

00:00:02.289 --> 00:00:05.723
This lesson is about capstone preview: ship something tiny.

00:00:05.723 --> 00:00:07.631
Graduation = shipped, not binge-watched.

00:00:07.631 --> 00:00:10.302
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:10.302 --> 00:00:14.117
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:14.117 --> 00:00:19.840
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:24.037
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:24.037 --> 00:00:29.760
Stay practical: define your tiny ship for week 2 before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:36.896
A tiny ship is small enough to finish in days: an offer draft, five outreaches, or one paid conversation.

00:00:36.896 --> 00:00:40.483
Remember the objective: define your tiny ship for week 2.

00:00:40.483 --> 00:00:44.429
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:44.429 --> 00:00:48.733
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:48.733 --> 00:00:52.679
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:52.679 --> 00:00:56.984
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:57.304 --> 00:01:00.154
Define your tiny ship for week two now.

00:01:00.154 --> 00:01:02.291
Write the deliverable in one sentence.

